---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy — Cutline" description="The Narge feed measures usage without storing addresses. No addresses, prefixes, or fetcher IDs are stored.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <section class="intro">
    <p class="lead">
      The Narge feed at <code>https://feeds.thecutline.org</code> measures usage without storing addresses. 
      The list is public, and no personal data is collected.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="what-we-measure">
    <h2>What Is Measured</h2>
    <p>
      The feed infrastructure counts distinct fetching addresses per ASN (Internet Service Provider) per UTC day.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Per ASN per day:</strong> How many distinct addresses from each ISP fetched the list today</li>
      <li><strong>No addresses stored:</strong> The address is dropped at once; only the daily count remains</li>
      <li><strong>k-threshold anonymization:</strong> Per-ASN counts are published only when ≥10 distinct addresses that day</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="how-it-works">
    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <p>
      When a firewall or DNS server fetches the feed, the Worker:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Reads the connecting address and ISP (ASN)</li>
      <li>Derives a one-day ID from the address (IPv6 addresses are reduced to their /64 prefix first)</li>
      <li><strong>Drops the address immediately</strong> — it is never written to storage</li>
      <li>Keeps the one-day ID in memory only until the day ends (for de-duplication)</li>
      <li>Increments the count for that ASN if this ID was not seen today</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      At midnight UTC, the daily counts are saved to storage and the in-memory IDs are discarded. 
      No address, prefix, or fetcher ID is ever written to disk.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="what-is-not-collected">
    <h2>What We Do Not Collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No addresses stored:</strong> Connecting addresses are dropped at once, never written to storage</li>
      <li><strong>No user accounts:</strong> No signup, no tokens required for the anonymous feed</li>
      <li><strong>No query names:</strong> The feed serves static files; we do not see what domains your firewall blocks</li>
      <li><strong>No device IDs:</strong> No cookies, no user-agent tracking, no fingerprinting</li>
      <li><strong>No browsing history:</strong> We serve a hostname list; we do not see your web traffic</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="retention">
    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fetcher IDs:</strong> Kept in memory only until the day ends, never stored</li>
      <li><strong>Daily counts:</strong> Per-ASN counts are kept indefinitely for public statistics</li>
      <li><strong>No address retention:</strong> Addresses are dropped at the edge and are not recoverable</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="public-stats">
    <h2>Public Statistics</h2>
    <p>
      Daily aggregated stats are published at <code>https://feeds.thecutline.org/stats.json</code>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Date and total fetch count</li>
      <li>Per-ASN rows: ISP name, distinct addresses, fetch count</li>
      <li>Rows are suppressed when &lt;10 distinct addresses that day (k-anonymity)</li>
      <li>Number of suppressed rows is disclosed</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If the counter is reset mid-day (rare), that day's distinct counts become upper bounds and the reset is disclosed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="per-org-tokens">
    <h2>Per-Organization Tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Organizations can request a unique feed URL token for attribution. The token identifies the organization 
      in internal logs (not published), but addresses are still dropped at once and not stored.
    </p>
    <p>
      The GitHub mirror (<code>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/...</code>) has no measurement at all.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="verification">
    <h2>How to Verify</h2>
    <p>
      The feed Worker code is public:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/tree/main/feeds-worker" target="_blank" rel="noopener">feeds-worker source code</a></li>
      <li>Privacy rules are enforced by tests: no addresses, prefixes, or fetcher IDs in storage</li>
      <li>Cloudflare Workers logs are off (<code>wrangler.toml</code> sets <code>observability.enabled = false</code>)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="no-business-model">
    <h2>No Data Sale</h2>
    <p>
      Cutline has no business model involving your data. No ads, no profiles, no sale to third parties. 
      This is a public feed with no charge to users.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="operator">
    <h2>Operator</h2>
    <p>
      The Narge feed and specification are maintained by <strong>Dov Allison</strong>. 
      For privacy questions or to report issues:
    </p>
    <p>
      Email: <a href="mailto:it@thecutline.org">it@thecutline.org</a><br>
      GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dov-max/narge-spec</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="more-info">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/privacy-design">Privacy Design</a> — Technical implementation details</li>
      <li><a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> — Legal terms and limitations</li>
      <li><a href="/for-it">For IT Teams</a> — How to use the feed</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  section {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }

  .intro {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul, ol {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  code {
    background: var(--color-text);
    color: #f8f8f2;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
